          <baseCommit>04002628f1cffde70188f74eb4c3a3607d9f6b24</baseCommit>
          <feedback>Stage 1 (&quot;Create Poem&quot;) completed as specified. The InstructionTask required creating/updating org.blockml.bml.workspace.playground.Poem.bml with a fresh random poem per execution. Execute replaced the prior &lt;documentation> content (a Chinese poem) with a new original English poem of two ABAB quatrains. Everything outside &lt;documentation> is preserved: block header/comment, namespaces, &lt;name>/&lt;type>/&lt;baseType> (playground:Poem / core:Documentation), &lt;is>, and all &lt;properties> (title=Poem, author=John Doe, year=2026). The change is minimal and scoped to the single expected file. No ModelTransformation or _meta/transform/ files were modified by Execute (the running/T00002_PoemTest_20260831T192003 block was only the pre-existing stage-start commit). Model remains structurally consistent and ready for Stage 2 (&quot;Translate Poem&quot;). Note: I could not run `npx blockml validate` (Bash disabled in this Reflect session), so validation was not independently re-confirmed, but the edit is well-formed XML consistent with the surrounding conventions.</feedback>
          <completedAt>2026-08-31T19:21:26</completedAt>
          <task>
            <composition>
              <workflow:InstructionTask instructions="Create or update the block org.blockml.bml.workspace.playground.Poem.bml that contains a random poem. For each execution create a new poem." />
